links-3252025">Economics Links, 3/25/2025</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.construction-physics.com/p/understanding-solar-energy?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.construction-physics.com/p/understanding-solar-energy?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Mar 2025 11:03:42 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[How Should We Think About the Economics of AI?]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>So, a break from political and policy madness. Along with everything else going on, there’s what looks like a revolutionary technology spreading through our society, which everyone calls AI, even though it doesn’t (yet?) look like the kind of artificial intelligence everyone expected…</p><p>URL: <a href="https://paulkrugman.substack.com/p/how-should-we-think-about-the-economics?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web">https://paulkrugman.substack.com/p/how-should-we-think-about-the-economics?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/economics-links-3252025">Economics Links, 3/25/2025</a></p>]]></description><link>https://paulkrugman.substack.com/p/how-should-we-think-about-the-economics?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://paulkrugman.substack.com/p/how-should-we-think-about-the-economics?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Mar 2025 11:03:42 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Inside the BTFP Subsidy]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>It has been two years since the banking “crisis” that claimed Silvergate, Signature, Silicon Valley Bank, and First Republic—and one year since the Federal Reserve stopped extending new “emergency” loans under the Bank Term Funding Program (BTFP). The final loans were repaid on March 11, 2025, and the Fed has since published a spreadsheet with the details. While the BTFP was not designed to print money for banks and credit unions, it effectively did so in November 2023-January 2024 before Fed officials…</p><p>URL: <a href="https://theovershoot.co/p/inside-the-btfp-subsidy?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web">https://theovershoot.co/p/inside-the-btfp-subsidy?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/economics-links-3252025">Economics Links, 3/25/2025</a></p>]]></description><link>https://theovershoot.co/p/inside-the-btfp-subsidy?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://theovershoot.co/p/inside-the-btfp-subsidy?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Mar 2025 11:03:42 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Social media isn't destroying society]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>One of the dominant narratives of our time is that social media is a technological wrecking ball responsible for everything bad in our society, including polarisation, misinformation, conspiracy theorising, attacks on democracy, collapsing trust in institutions…</p><p>URL: <a href="https://www.conspicuouscognition.com/p/social-media-isnt-destroying-society?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web">https://www.conspicuouscognition.com/p/social-media-isnt-destroying-society?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/social-learning-links-31d">Social Learning Links, 3/24/2025</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.conspicuouscognition.com/p/social-media-isnt-destroying-society?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.conspicuouscognition.com/p/social-media-isnt-destroying-society?utm_source=substack&a